Third-party dependencies

This project installs, but does not vendor, the following third-party
packages via pip (see requirements.txt) - each remains governed by its
own license, independent of the notice above:

* yt-dlp (https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp) - Unlicense (public domain).
* FastAPI (https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi) - MIT License.
* Uvicorn (https://github.com/encode/uvicorn) - BSD-3-Clause License.
* Pydantic (https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic) - MIT License.

This project also shells out to a system-installed ffmpeg binary (not
bundled or distributed with this repository) to merge/convert media -
ffmpeg's own license (LGPL/GPL, build-dependent) applies to that binary
independently. See https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.

---

Usage responsibility

This software is a general-purpose download client built on yt-dlp. It
does not circumvent DRM and does not target any specific platform's
technical protections. Whether downloading a given video is permitted
depends on that platform's own Terms of Service and applicable
copyright law, not on anything in this codebase - only download
content you own, that is in the public domain, or that you are
otherwise authorized to save a copy of.
